`resetTagsConfig` in main.ts is an unused import (only used in tests). tsconfig has no `noUnusedLocals`, so tsc doesn't flag it. Minor smell.

Also — importantly — `main.ts` imports `openAddDialog` from `./diary/ui/dialogs`, which pulls in a chain: dialogs → entries → panel... and panel → dialogs. Circular again, but they already exist in ui.

Now let me verify the panel-visible-on-load bug empirically. Let me write a tiny node script? Actually, easier: create a quick vitest one-off? That might be heavy. Let me reason again and also double check `init`:

```
export async function init(plugin?) {
  if (document.getElementById('diary-tag-filter')) {
    document.getElementById('diary-tag-filter')!.style.visibility = 'visible';
    const mask = document.getElementById('diary-filter-mask');
    if (mask) mask.style.visibility = 'visible';
    ...
    return;
  }
  ...
  createMaskAndPopup();
  createAddDialog();
  createConfirmDialog();
  createDatePicker();
  registerEscapeListener();

  if (state.ui.isPopupShown) {
    state.ui.maskLayer!.style.visibility = 'visible';
    state.ui.tagFilterPopup!.style.visibility = 'visible';
  } else {
    state.ui.isPopupShown = true;
  }
  ...
```

Yes — on very first init (fresh plugin load): `isPopupShown` = false → else branch: only sets flag, panel stays hidden. Bug confirmed by reading. The intent was clearly `if (!state.ui.isPopupShown)` → show + set true, OR simply always show.

Actually wait, let me reconsider the intent. In the original script the panel probably showed on load. The comment in main.ts: "初始化面板（与原宏行为一致：加载即打开）". So yes, bug.

However, the test file's 'ESC 关闭主面板' test asserts visible after init — which works only due to state leakage. Let me confirm: In beforeEach, `state.ui.isPopupShown` is NOT reset. Test 1 (面板创建) — after beforeEach init: isPopupShown false → set true, hidden. Test 1 passes (only checks existence). Test 2 (幂等) — init idempotent → visible. Test 3 (渲染卡片) — visible. Test 4 (ESC) — visible. So the test suite as a whole passes because of the leak. If a user ran only the ESC test in isolation, it would fail. This is a test-isolation smell AND masks the real bug.

Let me verify quickly by running a single test file or a specific test? vitest run with -t 'ESC'. Actually simpler: let me create a temporary test to check the fresh-load behavior. Hmm — but I shouldn't modify the repo. I can run a vitest filter on the ESC test alone. If it fails in isolation, that proves the leak dependence. Let me try.

Actually — running `npx vitest run -t "ESC 关闭主面板"` runs all files filtered by test name; beforeEach still runs init. Since each test file is a separate module instance, the ESC test would run in the panel.test.ts module — beforeEach init runs once → isPopupShown initially false → after init hidden → test asserts visible → FAIL. That would confirm the bug!

Let me try it.

